Interesting. If it's in fact the case that the model should trim both content and reasoning content, then the chat template is in fact the correct way to put it :) I'll try that and see if I can confirm the elimination of loops.

As for other models though, I wouldn't generalize. I remember some models have been actually *harmed* by truncating newlines (eg. the story of `:\n\n` I mentioned earlier - for Qwen `:\n\n` is actually a separate *token* and it's the one that drives the model to call a tool immediately after, so truncating this to `:\n` caused the model to suddenly be unable to call tools in later parts of an agentic session.

> then the chat template is in fact the correct way to put it

The fact that the official template doesn't probably means that they expect the inference engine should do as in #24985?

I'll have to see what the vLLM implementation does.

