}
```

I have a local version, but it's about 300 lines of slop code just to make the temporary file.

Also I haven't explored in-memory methods which would get around having to touch the disk.

that's not really a clean fix as writing a temp file will just burn the lifespan of SSD (for example on windows, tmp dir is not ramdisk)

if that's really the last solution, I'd prefer to first detect if MOOV is really at the end of file, then use the hack. otherwise, use in-memory file stream as usual

