query:
server: input_video reuses a previous request's decoded media when the prompt text repeats (video frames get no cache id)

## Summary
For OpenAI-compatible `input_video` requests, the server's prompt-cache prefix
comparison matches media chunks by id (`server-common.cpp`, `id_ai == id_bi`).
Image bitmaps get `id = hash_sha256_hex(buf, len)` — the code comments "use
sha256 to prevent cache poisoning". Video frame bitmaps are created in the
video helper (`mtmd-helper.cpp`, `read_next_frame`) with **no `set_id` call at
all**, so two frames from two different videos compare as `"" == ""` and match.
Send two completely different videos with identical instruction text and the
second request reuses the first's decoded media wholesale.

## Reproduction
Two 48-frame clips that cannot be confused (red field + yellow circle vs blue
field + green triangle), alternating requests, temperature 0, identical prompt
text:

    video + identical text:  8/8 described the WRONG video   (processed=4, cached=3112)
    video + unique text:     0/8 wrong                       (processed=3138, cached=0)
    stills + identical text: 0/8 wrong (ids compare media)   (cached=6416)

`processed=4` is the tell: essentially nothing was recomputed, so the media
came from another request's cache entry.

## Fix (verified; patch below)
Give the video helper a `source_id` — sha256 of the input buffer on the
`init_from_buf` path (the one the server uses), sha256 of the path string on
the path init (weaker, but not empty) — and stamp each frame bitmap with
`source_id + "#" + frame_index`. This is the identity images have always had,
extended to video frames.

## Impact
Any application sending repeated identical instruction text with different
videos silently receives descriptions of the wrong video. Templated prompts
make identical text the common case, not the corner.

Verified against a patched build: with the ids in place, the identical-prompt case goes 8/8 wrong → 0/8 wrong.

