thanks for the reply. I have tested the patch.

The simple io path of llama-cli is confirmed fixed: the program exits normally, other processes in the same console are no longer affected, and the spin you get when the output stays on the console is gone as well.

But the patch also brings some new problems.

First, model selection (list_and_ask_models in llama-cli): the old code treated an empty read as "ignore and ask again", now it aborts silently with exit code 1 and no message at all. Selecting a model by typing a number is not affected.

Second, a lone "/": it is popped off the line, so the reader returns an empty string, exactly what it returns on EOF, so after the patch typing "/" ends the session (it used to be ignored and the loop went on).

One consumer was missed: mtmd-cli. It does not check the return value of console::readline, it only watches g_is_interrupted, and on Windows it used to exit only because that broadcast interrupted it. With the broadcast gone it just spins forever once it reads EOF.

The "/" branch can add the newline before returning, the same way the "\" branch does, one place in the simple reader and one in the advanced reader. For mtmd-cli, a check that treats an empty read as EOF is enough.

