Its always one tile getting trashed and this patch fixes the issue, im not sure why there is a race here yet. cc @JohannesGaessler

The reduction between warps uses the same SRAM buffer as when loading the Q data. Without synchronization there is a race condition with the next tile. The `__syncthreads` can be optimized out if it is guaranteed that each memory location is only accessed by a single thread. This is the case for `np == 1` since there is a direct 1:1 correspondence between Q and VKQ columns. However, when I at some point added `nbatch_combine` I forgot that this can cause race conditions if `nbatch_combina != DKQ/2`. Does this patch fix the issue?

```diff
