I'd been trying to create a standalone repro for this in a project, but hadn't been able to narrow down what the trigger was, I can also confirm this bug on my own hardware. Thanks for figuring out the combination of settings that causes this problem 👍

Godot v4.8.dev6 - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 2 monitors (1920x1080 @ 240.00 Hz, 1920x1080 @ 59.94 Hz) - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX 6700 XT (Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; 32.0.21045.1000) - AMD Ryzen 7 5800X 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 31.92 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)

I had exactly the same problem; it's better to disable texture streaming or SDFGI. It is a dev build, after all.

Investigated this using claude.

Seems like ```RenderForwardClustered::_setup_render_pass_uniform_set``` was modified a couple of weeks ago to implement screen space contact shadows.
It was assigned a binding of 37 and binding for storage buffer was changed to 38.
In ```RenderForwardClustered::_setup_sdfgi_render_pass_uniform_set``` though, binding 37 is still being used for the storage buffer.

I was able to create a custom build by applying the following modification in ```RenderForwardClustered::_setup_sdfgi_render_pass_uniform_set```.

```
	{
		RD::Uniform u;
		u.binding = 37;    // Change this to 38
		u.uniform_type = RD::UNIFORM_TYPE_STORAGE_BUFFER;
		RID instance_buffer = scene_shader.default_material_feedback_buffer;
		u.append_id(instance_buffer);
		uniforms.push_back(u);
	}
```

**_NOTE: I am not sure if this modification is the proper way of fixing this issue. I defer to Godot maintainers for the correct fix._**

Cc @Rudolph-B

